A||||17||80's BOY||Did I Get Sprayed??? (N20)||||1||
Z||000000||80's BOY||09-19-2000||12:59 PM||||i was at a light when this ricer cavalier with a growth of a rear wing pulls up next to me. he starts talking smack, when all of a sudden the light turns green so i stick it to him hard.....like three car lengths. the next light comes up and he's revving again. what's with this ricer?? we take off and he kills me with speed i'd never imagine could come from a 4 banger cavalier. not even close, i mean my jaw just dropped. afterwards, being somewhat impressed i asked to see the engine. he said he doesn't show off his engine and it was just factory. BS!! i was looking in the interior for the nitrous switch but it was dark. what a ricer!! do ya'll think i got sprayed??||||reg||1
Z||000001||pollock||09-19-2000||01:18 PM||||I'd say so, dude, especially since he initiated it.<P>Just tell him to come up to Denton and square off on a silver 65 Mustang Fastback.<BR>I'll break him off somethin' strong...<P>Then i'll tell him i swapped an iron duke into it, but can't show him, since "my hood latch is broken."<BR><p>[This message has been edited by pollock (edited 09-19-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||HugGRRRFiero||09-19-2000||01:53 PM||||LOL... pollock, I gota agree.<P> <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>"HA, I just spanked you with my STOCK 4 cyl. Cavalier, NO you can't look under the hood... it's all stock anyway."<HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>What's this guy got too hide? a K&N filter?<P>Sounds like you caught him off guard at the first light.  Second light he was ready to squeeze the juice.<P>------------------<BR>         <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/huggrrr.gif">       <BR>       <A HREF="mailto:HugGRRRFiero@hotmail.com">HugGRRRFiero@hotmail.com</A> ||||reg||1
Z||000003||DjKid||09-19-2000||02:13 PM||||I think that nitrous users are pretty much saying.. "I can't beat you, so I'm gonna cheat."<P>------------------<BR>Ray - Blue 88 Coupe<BR><A HREF="http://blueknight.carolinafieros.com" TARGET=_blank>My Blue Knight</A> - <A HREF="http://www.carolinafieros.com" TARGET=_blank> Carolina Fieros</A>||||reg||1
Z||000004||HYPTNOTiSE||09-19-2000||02:27 PM||||Alright look, everyone talks about oh i want a supercharger, i want a turbo charger, i want a 3.4, i want a v-8.  You know what those all cost a lot more than 500-600 bucks correct?  So whats wrong with using nitrous to go fast?  All the big racers are doing it now, turbo with nitrous, supercharged with nitrous, lots of nitrous, the only guys that are naturally aspirated anymore, are they guys who have something to prove and have lots of money. If you want to go  fast and cheap you can't beat nitrous.  You say, it's not your engine doing the work? Screw that, it's all about cramming more and colder air in to the engine right?  super, turbo, and nitrous are all forced induction. going to a 3.4 is stroking the engine, thats just another way of cramming more air. dont cry cos you lost to someone who sprayed, if you really want to beat him, get a jug, get a turbo, get a supercharger. in the first place you have a v-6 he's got a 4cyl. he's gotta make the power up somewhere.  I remember i raced a taurus sho once on the street, in a 25-40mph zone. I thought for sure i'd have him.  I dont know if he had the jug or not but his car was super fast.  He'd drive alone nail it, both front tires would go up in smoke, and when he hit second, it seemed as the whole car would raise up and just plant the tires and roll them up in smoke, i mean bellowing from each wheel well.  I was going 125+ he had to be doing 140+mph, no joke, i was doing 125 and i wasn't even close he just kept pulling like i was sitting still.  Well that was before i had nitrous.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> just imagine the ticket if he got pulled over, yes sir i clocked you doing 145 in a 45mph zone, exceding the posted speed limit by 100mph. Sir you were over tripling the speed limit. Whew good thing we didn't get busted. <P>------------------<BR>       Mike LeCompte<BR>86 Fiero GT 3.2L w/ Nitrous<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.tcac.net/~daddyg/hypsig.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000005||80's BOY||09-19-2000||02:50 PM||||BTW HYP--thanks for the help....i'll be checking the mail everyday!!||||reg||1
Z||000006||HugGRRRFiero||09-19-2000||02:54 PM||||Hypnotise, I'm not saying it's wrong to use nitrous to improve horsepower.<P>What I'm saying is it's wrong to use nitrous against a fairly equally matched car, blow them away, then tell everyone your engine is stock and refuse to open the hood.  If he was actually using nitrous and just admited it flat out, I'd say cool cool, I'll buy a nitrous setup and we'll go head to head next week.<P>For example, it's illegal to run nitrous in a normally aspirated pro stock drag class.  It's not illegal in a sense because you can improve HP performance, but it gives an unfair advantage to the cheater.  Opening the hood I'd say would be the same as a quick tech inspection, and if he had nothing to hide he would have gladly opened the hood.<P>"Sure, I'll show you what's under the hood of my Fiero, but not my trunk, it's all stock."  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000007||Old Lar||09-19-2000||03:11 PM||||There was a Cavalier at the GTA show that sported a 3800 S/C under the hood.  If the 3800 s/c is a mover in a Fiero, I imagine it would be a mover in a Cavalier.||||reg||1
Z||000008||rockcrawl||09-19-2000||05:39 PM||||I've got a quick story for ya. My buddy is a mechanic at a local Chevy dealer. A new Cavalier came in one day with a bad engine noise. The car was on lease with 20k miles on the odometer. They tore it down and found pretty much everything inside was beyond repair. It needed a new engine, not a rebuild. They also found signs that a nitrous system was previously hooked up, and signs of the bottle being mounted in the trunk. It turns out the car was leased by some punk I graduated high school with, and he took it to the races on the weekends. No other mods, only the nitrous. Guess who paid for the new engine and labor! <P>The point of the story is that nitrous may not be so good for an otherwise stock engine. The engine is not designed to handle the excessive loads created by injecting nitrous. Sure the guy probably beat the piss out of it, but trashed at 20,000? Now take a 2.8 which has enough problems of it's own, and dump in some nitrous. Not me! Nitrous works in racing, because it's used with engines that are built for racing.<P>------------------<BR>Jon Lagler<BR>'86 GT 3800 (for sale)<BR>'87 GT (noisey 2.8)<BR>4.9 liter V8 Testarossa Spyder (under construction)||||reg||1
Z||000009||1FST2M6||09-19-2000||09:14 PM||||i went through 16 bottles in a little bit over 6 months and never once had a nitrous related problem... (problems - clutch x4, bad Crane Hi-6 box, and brake pads like they're going out of style, and tires) 4 months after i took my bottle off is when i had an engine problem.. and that wasn't nitrous related either.. it was oil related. Nitrous is fun, cheap and easy.. just make sure if you SMOKE some unsuspecting person you make sure and give the credit to the bottle... not "well your car just sucks and i'm all stock" i've been beat by kids with nitrous before.. they all claim "dude it's stock" til they need springs put on or somthing like that and they come to the shop... "oh i just last night put that on" ok kid.. what ever...  ||||reg||1
Z||000010||Shaun41178||09-20-2000||01:08 AM||||I live in the nitrous camp but I am tired of argueing for our side.  Everyone says it will blow up a engine if the engine is not built for it.  Well believe what you want I guess.  I have had no problems with having nitrous on my car and for two years as well.  If you think nitrous is cheating then fine.  If you don't think it is cheating then fine.  If you think it is cheating cause you don't understand it and how it works then fine.  Either way, fine.  I was able to afford a nitrous kit so i got one.  I was not able to afford a turbo kit so I got nitrous.  I was not able to afford a supercharger kit so I got nitrous.  I was not able to afford a V8 so I got nitrous.  I was not able to afford an engine swap of any sort so I got nitrous.  See where I am going with this?  Nitrous is easy hp and inexpensive too.<P>But yea that guy was probably spraying you or not even racing the first time.  You sure he had a 4 cyl or a v6?  I am guessing you have a 6?  If you had a 6 and he had a 4cyl and he is juicing it, he still shouldn't have beaten you as bad as you say he did.  Well I guess that depends on what year that Cavalier was.  I know the new ones can have 150 hp depending on what engine they have.  With that engine and nitrous he would smoke you bad.<P>I never tell people that I have nitrous unless they specifically ask if I have nitrous.  I once had a guy in a 95 GT Mustang ask me if I had a blower on my car.  I of course told him I didn't.  I didn't tell him what I had, I just told him enough to andswer his question.  Thats one of the best things about racing.  I beat some guy in some hot Mustang or Camaro and they ask me simple questions like "is that a V6?"  I say yep.  They never ask specifics so I don't tell them any.  It gets them thinking how they got beat and its funny to see them looking at your car trying to figure out how they lost.  Its a priceless look.  <P>------------------<BR>Shaun-Toledo OH, 85 GT<BR>3.2 With nitrous<BR>http://members.aol.com/shaun41178||||reg||1
Z||000011||ThatRickGuy||09-20-2000||10:10 AM||||I wouldn't be upset about being beaten by someone with nitrous, but I would be upset if they were claiming that thier "stock" vehicle blew mine away. I mean, if I went up against a '00 corvette, sure, he would blow my doors off. but would he go home bragging about how he roasted an '88 fiero? That'd be like me bragging about killing a '72 vw bug. And as for nitrious in my car... after $1800 worth of work... no way, maybe when I have enough cash to just have a spare car to drive for fun, but not when it's my daily driver.||||reg||1
Z||000012||Eric_PA||09-20-2000||01:05 PM||||80's boy, was it a new style cav Z-24 with the 2.4 twin cam. I have Sunfire GT with <BR> the 2.4 with minor bolt ons and an aftermarket clutch. It is way faster than my fiero. But my Fiero is an automatic so that's not a good comparison. If it is that engine, it is rated for 150 HP and 155 ft#'s of torque. I have surprised many people with mine. This car has made me decide to put a Quad in my Fiero since they run so well. The 2.4 twin cam is a newer version of the older Quad 4's some of which in the past where rated for 180HP.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000013||80's BOY||09-20-2000||04:05 PM||||yeah, it was a new z-24. but my guess is still like many others. he wasn't armed at the first light and thought he could take me. then after he got his juice ready, he went for it the next go around. i mean, who out of all motorheads puts that much attention into a vehicle, and then won't even open the hood??? i open my hood every chance i get because i'm proud of what i've done. stupid ricer probably had his japanese decals on upside down anyway!! it's an american made car for God's sake!! red with yellow scallops. the "McDonald's Racer" that's what he looks like. next time i'll ask him if ne wants fries with that!!||||reg||1
Z||000014||whamel||09-20-2000||04:27 PM||||FYI - I have (and have had) a couple good cars that I refuse to open the hood on, I like the mystery.  But believe me - I make no claim that those cars are stock..they are VERY far from stock.  I'm not trying to give you a tough time 80's boy - I just live in a very competitive area and I do street race.  <P>Also, I don't understand why everybody says Nitrous is 'cheating'?  What makes it cheating?  Is it because it's not obvious?<BR>Thanks,  <BR>Wade<P> <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>, who out of all motorheads puts that much attention into a vehicle, and then won't even open the hood??? [/B]<HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>||||reg||1
Z||000015||Seanh||09-20-2000||05:18 PM||||Iv looked into Nitro's but the people told me that I shouldnt go with it on the 2.8 V6 engine in my car. They said that it could blow your engine if you hit it at the wrong time. Has anyone put Nitro's on a stock 2.8? Have you had any trouble? Would it be recommened that I do it? ||||reg||1
Z||000016||olympic||09-21-2000||02:11 AM||||I have a quick question for the nitrous experts.  Can you safely use nitrous on a stick shift car?  I'm thinking the engine might grenade when you let off the gas to shift gears.  Whereas an automatic you just hold it to the floor until the race is over.  I know you can hook your nitrous up so its only spraying when your at WOT but I'm still just wondering......||||reg||5
Z||000017||1FST2M6||09-21-2000||08:35 AM||||yes you can use it on a stick shift car.. yes you can use it on a stock 2.8! The only real engine mod i had was Si valves... the bottom end had 96k miles on it.. and i STILL went through 16+ bottles with NO problems. my car was a 4spd (3:65 final drive) as long as you have enough fuel you'll be hard pressed to have a nitrous related problem. after about 2 weeks of not being impressed with the nitrous kit i changed jets and injectors and was able to stomp just about anything from light to light.. but i had a weak top end. (she'd fall on her face in 4th) it was a TORQUE monster but only had a 40hp shot... if you look at the dyno sheets... Shaun41178 has a stock motor running 14.1 in an automatic.. so yes they can handle the abuse.    ||||reg||1
